# Day 3 – Challenges

## Challenges Faced

* Understanding the differences between Validation Rules, Flows, and Apex Triggers.
* Configuring Record-Triggered Flows correctly.
* Setting field values automatically using Flow.
* Creating and testing Validation Rules.
* Troubleshooting Flow execution and record creation.
* Understanding the order of execution of Salesforce automation.

## How I Solved Them

* Used Flow Builder to configure Record-Triggered Flows.
* Tested flows with multiple Application records.
* Verified Validation Rules using different test scenarios.
* Reviewed Flow execution paths and corrected configuration issues.
* Compared declarative automation with Apex to choose the appropriate solution.

## Lessons Learned

* Use Validation Rules to validate user input.
* Use Flows for automation without writing code.
* Use Apex only when business logic is too complex for declarative tools.
* Choosing the right automation tool improves maintainability and performance.
